{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Fuaran deterministic GFM markdown-render conformance corpus (Phase 292). Each fixture pins a markdown `source` to the canonical rendered `html` every Fuaran host (F#/Fable client, Renderer.Server, TS @fuaran-ui/renderer, Python fuaran_py.renderer) must reproduce byte-for-byte. The F# renderer (Fuaran.UI.Renderer.Markdown.toHtml in Renderer.Core) is the reference; a gate-test in each host asserts render(source) == html for every entry, so a one-byte divergence in any host turns the gate red. Feature coverage tracks the GFM spec (github.github.com/gfm) at the common-case bar; see fuaran-dotnet/docs/MARKDOWN.md for the IN/OUT/DEFERRED buckets. Phase 1032: a fixture MAY carry a ``policy`` naming the destination policy the render is performed under — ``permissive`` (the default when the field is absent; every destination the scheme floor accepts is emitted as authored, which is the pure string-to-string function this corpus has pinned since Phase 292), ``denyNonLocal`` (the default a decoded tree gets: same-origin allowed, every absolute network origin and every hostless scheme refused), or ``declaredExample`` (denyNonLocal plus an exact-host rule for cdn.example scoped to media and a host-suffix rule for docs.example scoped to hyperlink — so class scoping and label-boundary suffix matching are pinned too). A policy is HOST-CONSTRUCTED: the corpus names one, it never carries one as data. A refused destination renders about:blank#fuaran-egress-refused plus a data-fuaran-egress-refused attribute, appended LAST, whose value is the egress class and the host — never the path or the query. See WIRE_FORMAT.md section 14.1.",
